nt differences, then\n  the nested ternary. Note C's `abs(INT_MIN)` is not reachable here.\n- division: C `/` on ints truncates toward zero; operands here are non-negative.\n- pointer arithmetic and the exact place where `raw++` / `png->p +=` happens\n  relative to the reads (`switch (*raw++)` reads the filter byte and THEN\n  advances, so all later `raw[x]` indices are relative to the byte AFTER the\n  filter byte).\n- `cp_unfilter`'s loop epilogue: `for (int y = 1; y < h; y++, prev = raw, raw += len)`.\n  The comma-expression runs AFTER the body, and `raw` at that point has ALREADY\n  been advanced by 1 (the filter byte). Confirm the Rust reproduces the exact\n  same `prev`/`raw` values on every iteration, including the initial\n  `prev = raw; raw += len;` before the loop.\n- `cp_chunk`: `int offset = len + 12;` — `len` is `uint32_t`, so `len + 12`\n  wraps as uint32_t and is then CONVERTED to `int` (implementation-defined for\n  values > INT_MAX). Then `png->p + offset` uses the int (so a negative offset\n  moves backwards). Check the Rust does the identical two-step conversion.\n- `cp_find`: `png->p += len + 12;` — here the addend is `uint32_t` (no int\n  variable), so the pointer advances by a value that is zero-extended, NOT\n  sign-extended, on a 64-bit target. Check whether the Rust matches; the Rust\n  currently writes `.wrapping_offset(len.wrapping_add(12) as c_int as isize)`\n  which SIGN-extends via `as c_int`. Determine whether that is a divergence from\n  the C, and if it is, fix the Rust.\n- `cp_chunk` / `cp_find` use `memcmp(start + 4, chunk, 4)` and test `!memcmp(...)`\n  — i.e. equality of 4 bytes. Verify the Rust helper `cp_memcmp4` is used with\n  the same operand order and the same `!= 0` sense.\n- the exact `return 0` / `return 1` / `return NULL` values and the order of the\n  `&&` short-circuit conditions.\n\nReport back a concise table: function | verdict (MATCH / DIVERGENCE) | if\ndivergence, the exact C line, the exact Rust line, and what you changed. If you\nchange anything, make the minimal edit to /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-TrEEjg/translation/src/lib.rs\nonly, keeping the existing style (wrapping_* helpers, no bounds checks added).\nDo not touch anything outside those five functions."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1762,"cache_read_input_tokens":205931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1762,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a545b5b-9a0e-47ab-b3c0-3ce9bc5f969e","uuid":"b2149496-30c7-4724-97c5-a3d925becf2e","timestamp":"2026-09-05T07:30:28.294Z"}
