{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015fZT3pSoiciFaHmcy5NtwN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/` (a stripped-down `cute_png`).\n2\t//!\n3\t//! The translation is deliberately literal: it mirrors the C control flow,\n4\t//! integer widths, wrap-around arithmetic, pointer arithmetic and the exact\n5\t//! order of validation checks.  Bugs present in the original C are reproduced\n6\t//! rather than fixed.\n7\t//!\n8\t//! Exported ABI (matches `nm -D` on the C shared object):\n9\t//!   * `convert_pix`            (function)\n10\t//!   * `cp_inflate`             (function)\n11\t//!   * `cp_error_reason`        (data, `const char *`)\n12\t//!   * `cp_fixed_table`         (data, `uint8_t[288+32]`)\n13\t//!   * `cp_permutation_order`   (data, `uint8_t[19]`)\n14\t//!   * `cp_len_extra_bits`      (data, `uint8_t[29+2]`)\n15\t//!   * `cp_len_base`            (data, `uint32_t[29+2]`)\n16\t//!   * `cp_dist_extra_bits`     (data, `uint8_t[30+2]`)\n17\t//!   * `cp_dist_base`           (data, `uint32_t[30+2]`)\n18\t\n19\t#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n20\t#![allow(non_upper_case_globals)]\n21\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n22\t#![allow(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]\n23\t#![allow(dead_code)]\n24\t\n25\tuse std::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n26\tuse std::ptr;\n27\t\n28\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n29\t// assert() emulation\n30\t//\n31\t// The reference C library is compiled by the supplied CMakeLists.txt without\n32\t// NDEBUG, so `assert()` is live and a failing assertion terminates the process\n33\t// with SIGABRT.  Reproduce that: report on stderr, then abort.\n34\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n35\t\n36\t/// Absolute path of `c_src/src/lib.c`, as cmake hands it to the C compiler\n37\t/// (`__FILE__`).  Supplied by `build.rs`.\n38\tconst CP_C_FILE: &str = env!(\"CP_C_SOURCE_PATH\");\n39\t\n40\tuns