hile the C is fine — the test has teeth.\n\n## Phase artifacts (crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — symbol diff is **empty**: C exports 9 symbols, Rust exports the same 9, no extras. Undefined symbols are libc/platform only.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 37 rows, all 25 checklist items passing. 6 `cp_error_reason` rejections, 9 `assert`/`SIGABRT` paths, 12 helper rejections, FFI boundaries (null/zero/negative lengths, out-of-range `bpp` incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`), plus 2 documented non-assertable UB/non-terminating inputs.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 41 rows, all passing: 4 input alignments × 4 tail lengths, all 3 block types, chained blocks, every length/distance bucket, `memset` vs overlapping copy, code-length RLE 16/17/18 and none, HLIT/HDIST/HCLEN extremes, codes >9 bits, all 10 zlib levels, 64 KiB payloads, mutated exported tables.\n\n## Test suite (81 tests, passing in dev **and** release)\n\n`valid.rs` 38 · `errors.rs` 14 · `aborts.rs` 10 · `private.rs` 7 · `coverage.rs` 3 · `symbols.rs` 3 · `tamper.rs` 2 · `risky.rs` 2 · `feature_matrix.rs` 2. Everything goes through `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n\nNotable techniques needed to reach full coverage:\n- A **hand-written DEFLATE encoder** — `flate2` never emits a fixed block and gives no control over HLIT/HDIST/HCLEN, RLE symbols, or code lengths >9 bits.\n- **Child-process differentials** for the 5 `assert` paths, comparing terminating signal *and* byte-identical glibc `__assert_fail` stderr (file, line, function, assertion text).\n- **Local-symbol address recovery** for the 5 `static` helpers that no exported symbol reaches: `c_src` builds at `-O0`, so they survive in `.symtab`; `base = dlsym(\"cp_inflate\") - nm_offset(\"cp_inflate\")`. The Rust side uses a test-only `private_probe` cdylib. This is what caught the `cp_find` bug.\n- A **global mutex** — `cp_error_reason` is one mutable global per `.so`, and parallel tests were clobbering each other.\n\n## C quirks confirmed as ground truth (reproduced, not \"fixed\")\n\n- `cp_peak_bits` adds `bits_left` instead of the *unbuffered* bit count when folding in `final_word`, so `cp_ptr` is off and **stored blocks decode from the wrong offset** whenever `(in_bytes - first_bytes) % 4 != 0`. Payload round-trip is asserted only for word-aligned shapes; C/Rust equality always.\n- `cp_stored` has **no `out_end` check at all**, and its `LEN` check only bounds from below — a large `LEN` over-reads the input and over-writes the output buffer (row 40).\n- `cp_error_reason` is never cleared on success.\n- `cp_find` loops forever on a chunk length of `0xFFFFFFF4` (`len + 12` wraps to 0) — recorded, not asserted, since both hang identically.\n\n`./run_all_configs.sh` enumerates feature combinations from `Cargo.toml` and runs the suite in both profiles: **6 configurations, all passing**. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only `c_src/build/` added by the prescribed cmake commands).","ttft_ms":3485,"type":"result","duration_ms":3893743,"uuid":"73a71282-9920-4268-81da-75b45eae7585","ttft_stream_ms":3346,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":3346,"queued_turn_count":0}
